  },
  {
    "episode_id": 66284,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66284.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "And every year we have to produce the federal spending for the upcoming fiscal year. We do that in 12 separate bills ranging from defense to justice, to housing, to transportation, to foreign affairs, and everywhere in between. And we have been here in Washington this week, although the full house is not in session. The appropriations committee has been meeting every day all day to crunch through those bills. And we just finished the last bill just about just about half an hour ago, as a matter of fact, it's been a full week for me here. I've certainly been trying to pursue not only programs that are of benefit to our country and make the right decisions there, but a specific benefit to what you cross the board. One area, for example, would be in defense. Of course, our defense presence in Hawaii is not only something that I think we owe to our country, but it is our second economic generator. And in fact, for the last year and a half, it's been our number one economic generator, so to consider a Hawaii that had both tourism go down without the backstop of defenses to consider far more of a disaster than we saw. And so from that perspective, I've been involved, for example, in trying to maintain funding to improve Pearl Harbor Naval Shipyard, our largest industrial employer, which is a key economic driver for our Hawaii. Other areas would include native Hawaiian education, native Hawaiian healthcare, certainly our business communities, help to tourism, transportation and the infrastructure, our ports, our harbors. It's really been a week in which I not only took a broad range of of views across the entire federal government. But how could I get the federal government through the appropriations process to attend to what is specific needs, both specific to Hawaii but also to the Indo-Pacific?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
