    "turn_text": "want to ask you, I know that it's not necessarily in the federal purview to set this policy, but Governor David Ige is holding fast at his benchmark of 70% fully vaccinated. He's counting the entire population. That includes children under 12 who cannot access the vaccine. to get to that 70%. There's been some pushback here locally against that. But even in the comments right now, there are some people who are saying the cases are going up, we're not doing well. So there are a lot of concerns. What are your thoughts on the indoor mask mandate here in the islands? Do you agree with the governor for holding fast to that 70%?",
