  {
    "episode_id": 66284,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66284.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, on one level, yes, of course it's tempting because there are many, many challenges that Hawaii faces that really cannot be solved at the federal level. I mean, I can help, but the state and county government levels are where those decisions are made. And sure, I think about taking a shot at helping my state at that level. I think my better utility, my best utility for Hawaii, where I can most help Hawaii, given my experience and my seniority and my time in Washington, especially as our delegation goes through some transition with Congressman Kelly coming on, although he's doing incredible in terms of his first six months. I just think my best utility for what he is here. I have filed my papers for re-election the next time around. I guess I'm at the point in my life when I never say absolutely not because I've said absolutely not before and then hasn't worked out that way. But that's what I'm doing. I'm not a candidate for governor. I'm not trying to be the governor. I'm certainly interested in it. And I certainly hope that the candidates that step forward for Governor are candidates that I think can lead a change in a way that is needed at the state and the local level.",
