  {
    "episode_id": 66284,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66284.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think the first thing obviously is Everybody knows this. We're not out of COVID-19, not by a long shot. It's going to be with us. I will state very frontally that I believe that vaccinations are the way forward. We know that 98% of the people that are getting sick in Hawaii right now are unfaccinated and are getting sick from other people that are not unfaccinated, but there are people that are vaccinated that are being exposed and getting sick. So I think this is where we need to go. We need to keep up the good work that we've already done. That is still our answer in the midterm at least. So that's the first thing I would say. And the second thing I would say is that again, as it has been for 17 months of a terrible crisis, my office is completely open. to anybody that does have any questions. I don't care whether it's a, you know, I don't care whether there aren't any stupid questions. I mean, people say that, but I promise there are no stupid questions. We want to help. We're here to help, and the best way into my office is case.house.gov, case.house.gov.",
